WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.040 --> 00:00:05.270
Part 3 of Chilling Adventures of Sabrina is
stuffed with easter eggs, hidden references

00:00:05.270 --> 00:00:07.620
and monstrous secrets buried in each episode.

00:00:07.620 --> 00:00:08.840
Yippee-ki-yay, movie lovers!

00:00:08.840 --> 00:00:13.809
I'm Jan and in this video I'm revealing 28
devilish details you might have missed in

00:00:13.809 --> 00:00:18.590
Chilling Adventures Season 3, including the
Riverdale easter eggs that reveal a very weirdly

00:00:18.590 --> 00:00:19.720
connected universe.

00:00:19.720 --> 00:00:23.390
There will, of course, be spoilers so take
care if you haven't caught up.

00:00:23.390 --> 00:00:28.500
Part 3 opens with Sabrina's terrifying nightmare
of wandering into Hell and discovering Nick

00:00:28.500 --> 00:00:30.000
encased in stone.

00:00:30.000 --> 00:00:34.460
It's a clever bit of foreshadowing for Sabrina's
own fate later in the season when she gets

00:00:34.460 --> 00:00:37.560
trapped in the Ninth Circle of Hell by Caliban.

00:00:37.560 --> 00:00:41.770
It's not until the seventh episode that Robin
reveals he's a hobgoblin to Theo.

00:00:41.770 --> 00:00:45.890
But there was a clue to his true identity
all the way back in the fourth episode when

00:00:45.890 --> 00:00:50.210
Carcosa called Robin by his full name:
"Thank you for warning us Robin Goodfellow."

00:00:50.210 --> 00:00:54.150
The name "Robin Goodfellow" is often used
in English folklore for a mischievous sprite

00:00:54.150 --> 00:00:58.280
or hobgoblin, and in English mythology and
literature such as Shakespeare's A Midsummer

00:00:58.280 --> 00:01:02.300
Night's Dream, Robin Goodfellow also goes
by the name of "Puck".

00:01:02.300 --> 00:01:05.760
Chilling Adventures begins to introduce new
Lovecraftian monsters into its universe when

00:01:05.760 --> 00:01:10.810
Blackwood calls upon an amphibian-like beast
to rise out of the waters of Loch Ness.

00:01:10.810 --> 00:01:15.290
Blackwood calls the creature the "Deep One",
the same name as a species of water-dwelling

00:01:15.290 --> 00:01:16.580
monsters from H.P.

00:01:16.580 --> 00:01:19.250
Lovecraft's novella The Shadow Over Innsmouth.

00:01:19.250 --> 00:01:23.830
And another of Lovecraft's sci-fi horrors
is referenced when Zelda weighs up the covens'

00:01:23.830 --> 00:01:26.570
options to avoid getting killed by the pagans.

00:01:26.570 --> 00:01:29.180
"We could flee perhaps to the Mountains of
Madness."

00:01:29.180 --> 00:01:33.740
"At the Mountains of Madness" is a novella
by Lovecraft that features a dangerous alien

00:01:33.740 --> 00:01:38.760
civilisation in Antarctica that lies beyond
a mountain range even higher than the Himalayas.

00:01:38.760 --> 00:01:43.950
And the word Carcosa, the name of the malevolent
carnival leader who arrives in Greendale,

00:01:43.950 --> 00:01:49.490
first appeared in several 19th-century short
stories as an ancient mysterious city before

00:01:49.490 --> 00:01:54.150
being used as the name of an alien city within
the Lovecraftian Cthulhu Mythos.

00:01:54.150 --> 00:02:00.119
In that universe, Carcosa is home to Hastur,
a monstrous deity who's also known as "The

00:02:00.119 --> 00:02:03.920
Unspeakable One", something which ties in
to how Blackwood describes the Eldritch Terrors

00:02:03.920 --> 00:02:06.860
he plans to bring into the world.

00:02:06.860 --> 00:02:10.659
"Return to me the egg, and we'll bear witness
to the birth of the unspeakable."

00:02:10.659 --> 00:02:16.480
Carcosa and the pagans plan to resurrect their
Old Gods in an event they call The Great Flowering.

00:02:16.480 --> 00:02:21.310
For the ceremony, they place a sacrificial
virgin inside a giant green plant statue,

00:02:21.310 --> 00:02:25.450
much like the virgin sacrifice that a group
of pagans carry out inside a giant wicker

00:02:25.450 --> 00:02:29.040
man statue in the 1973 horror movie The Wicker
Man.

00:02:29.040 --> 00:02:34.239
And the pagans in Greendale also wear animal
masks at the coven's Hare Moon celebration,

00:02:34.239 --> 00:02:36.409
just like the pagans do in The Wicker Man.

00:02:36.409 --> 00:02:41.019
At the carnival, the Ferris wheel that Theo
and Robin ride is called "The Berlanti Wheel",

00:02:41.019 --> 00:02:45.900
an easter egg to prolific TV producer Greg
Berlanti, whose shows include Chilling Adventures,

00:02:45.900 --> 00:02:48.950
Riverdale, Arrow, Supergirl, and You.

00:02:48.950 --> 00:02:53.400
This season also includes several references
to the modern horror movie "Midsommar" about

00:02:53.400 --> 00:02:54.760
a pagan cult.

00:02:54.760 --> 00:02:59.069
In Chilling Adventures, when Sabrina returns
to find the pagans have created an apocalypse

00:02:59.069 --> 00:03:04.299
on Earth, she's startled by a couple of plant-like
human zombies, who appear to have a pair of

00:03:04.299 --> 00:03:06.590
yellow flowers growing in their eyes.

00:03:06.590 --> 00:03:12.760
This is a creepy nod to one of the pagan human
sacrifices in the movie.

00:03:12.760 --> 00:03:19.040
In fact, Sabrina showrunner Roberto Aguirre-Sacasa
has specifically said that films like that

00:03:19.040 --> 00:03:22.889
and The Wicker Man were 'always the kind of
horror that [he] wanted to get to play with

00:03:22.889 --> 00:03:25.340
and infuse into Part 3.'

00:03:25.340 --> 00:03:29.069
And the flower crowns the Greendale coven
wear for The Hare Moon festival, which are

00:03:29.069 --> 00:03:34.219
an ancient tradition used in many pagan ceremonies,
also recently appeared in Midsommar.

00:03:34.219 --> 00:03:38.950
After arriving in Hell, Sabrina asks Caliban
how they can get to Pandemonium, and he answers:

00:03:38.950 --> 00:03:43.519
"Follow the blood-red road where it flows,
and there you'll find the throne of Hell."

00:03:43.519 --> 00:03:48.129
That advice is a bloody reference to The Wizard
of Oz and the Good Witch of the North's instructions

00:03:48.129 --> 00:03:50.579
to Dorothy on how to reach the Emerald City.

00:03:50.579 --> 00:03:54.089
"All you do is follow the yellow brick road."

00:03:54.089 --> 00:03:58.409
And like Dorothy in the Wizard of Oz, Sabrina
and the gang also come across their own Tin

00:03:58.409 --> 00:04:03.430
Man in the form of Tommy, Harvey's brother
who died in the first season of Chilling Adventures.

00:04:03.430 --> 00:04:07.459
Like the classic movie's Tin Man, Tommy also
has problems with his heart.

00:04:07.459 --> 00:04:12.139
But while the original Tin Man believed he
lacked a heart, Tommy's heart is on the outside

00:04:12.139 --> 00:04:14.019
of his tin costume.

00:04:14.019 --> 00:04:17.100
Another classic tale is referenced in Hell's
Forest of Torment.

00:04:17.100 --> 00:04:20.780
When Sabrina and Roz go to pick the Fleur
du Mal that Dorian Gray has asked them to

00:04:20.780 --> 00:04:24.850
collect, Sabrina warns her friend that if
they prick themselves on the flower's thorns,

00:04:24.850 --> 00:04:27.170
they'll go to sleep and never wake up.

00:04:27.170 --> 00:04:31.150
That was also the fate of the princess in
Sleeping Beauty when she pricked her finger

00:04:31.150 --> 00:04:32.520
on a cursed spinning wheel.

00:04:32.520 --> 00:04:35.250
"It's like something out of a fairy tale."

00:04:35.250 --> 00:04:39.790
And remember that princess Aurora was also
known by the prickly, flowery name of Briar

00:04:39.790 --> 00:04:40.790
Rose.

00:04:40.790 --> 00:04:45.000
Also in Chilling Adventures, the flower even
sings and calls to Sabrina and Roz luring

00:04:45.000 --> 00:04:49.430
them into a potential trap, similar to how
Maleficent entranced and tricked Aurora into

00:04:49.430 --> 00:04:51.070
pricking herself.

00:04:51.070 --> 00:04:55.280
And later, after they bring Nick back from
Hell to the mortal world, Sabrina wakes him

00:04:55.280 --> 00:04:59.820
with a kiss, akin to how Sleeping Beauty was
woken from her curse.

00:04:59.820 --> 00:05:04.100
The evil flower that Dorian Gray asks Sabrina
to get for him is also a reference to a set

00:05:04.100 --> 00:05:07.760
of poems by Charles Baudelaire called "Les
Fleurs du Mal".

00:05:07.760 --> 00:05:11.930
Appropriately for Chilling Adventures, Baudelaire's
collection of poems includes one called "The

00:05:11.930 --> 00:05:16.950
Litanies of Satan" which fiercely criticised
the 19th-century Church and also inverted

00:05:16.950 --> 00:05:21.660
several prayers from the Catholic Mass and
substituted Mary's name with Satan's.

00:05:21.660 --> 00:05:25.510
Likewise, Chilling Adventures also likes to
flip common religious expressions:

00:05:25.510 --> 00:05:26.850
"In other words..

00:05:26.850 --> 00:05:28.230
Back the heaven off."

00:05:28.230 --> 00:05:32.560
And in Part 3, Zelda's prayer "Hail Lilith"
is an inversion of the traditional Catholic

00:05:32.560 --> 00:05:34.190
prayer "Hail Mary".

00:05:34.190 --> 00:05:36.470
"Hail Lilith, full of disgrace.

00:05:36.470 --> 00:05:40.440
Cursed are you amongst women, and cursed is
the fruit of thy womb, demons."

00:05:40.440 --> 00:05:45.220
Sabrina manages to reverse the pagan apocalypse,
but in the process she also decides to allow

00:05:45.220 --> 00:05:48.030
a double of herself to exist at the same time.

00:05:48.030 --> 00:05:52.480
This twin Sabrina situation is something that
already occurred in the 90s sitcom Sabrina

00:05:52.480 --> 00:05:53.910
The Teenage Witch.

00:05:53.910 --> 00:05:58.660
At the end of the third season of the old-school
show, Sabrina met her identical twin Katrina

00:05:58.660 --> 00:06:02.630
and they had to undergo a test to find out
which sibling was the evil one.

00:06:02.630 --> 00:06:06.620
When the test revealed that Sabrina's sister
Katrina was the evil sibling, Katrina was

00:06:06.620 --> 00:06:10.920
sent to live in the Twin Cities in a place
known as the "Other Realm".

00:06:10.920 --> 00:06:14.930
While one Sabrina returns to Greendale in
Chilling Adventures, the other goes to Hell

00:06:14.930 --> 00:06:18.830
where Lilith prepares her for her full-time
role as Queen of Hell.

00:06:18.830 --> 00:06:22.610
Sabrina's style, including her coronation
dress and white makeup, evoke the look of

00:06:22.610 --> 00:06:27.550
English Tudor monarch Elizabeth I, who was
known as "the Virgin Queen" and whose reign

00:06:27.550 --> 00:06:30.700
included the attempted invasion of England
by the Spanish Armada.

00:06:30.700 --> 00:06:35.530
On top of that, Sabrina's coronation seems
to pay specific homage to the final scene

00:06:35.530 --> 00:06:40.150
of the late-90s movie Elizabeth, with each
queen's people bowing down to her and touching

00:06:40.150 --> 00:06:45.030
her dress, and the queen signalling her ascent
to the throne with a little hand gesture.

00:06:45.030 --> 00:06:50.060
The parallels between Queen Elizabeth I and
Queen Sabrina of Hell become even more striking

00:06:50.060 --> 00:06:53.930
when Lilith speaks to Sabrina about what's
in store for the new young queen.

00:06:53.930 --> 00:06:56.360
"Every queen must be made battle-ready.

00:06:56.360 --> 00:06:58.200
Every girl must prepare for war.

00:06:58.200 --> 00:06:59.580
Let nothing touch you.

00:06:59.580 --> 00:07:01.780
Let no man hold power over you."

00:07:01.780 --> 00:07:07.240
And emphasising that at least Hell-bound Sabrina
will be uninterested in love, Sabrina tells

00:07:07.240 --> 00:07:08.240
Lucifer.

00:07:08.240 --> 00:07:12.180
"I am ready, Father, to be married to Hell."

00:07:12.180 --> 00:07:16.410
Much as Elizabeth I was considered as being
wed to her kingdom.

00:07:16.410 --> 00:07:21.510
In Part 3, Ambrose plays a key part in events
when he and Prudence track down Father Blackwood

00:07:21.510 --> 00:07:24.280
who's gone into hiding in Loch Ness, Scotland.

00:07:24.280 --> 00:07:27.920
When they arrive, Ambrose explains that he
already has some knowledge of the location:

00:07:27.920 --> 00:07:30.990
"Loch Ness lies atop a powerful rift along
the Earth's ley lines.

00:07:30.990 --> 00:07:34.950
Aleister Crowley himself once harnessed its
energies for his own higher magicks."

00:07:34.950 --> 00:07:38.940
Ambrose's familiarity with Crowley's life
stems from a time when Crowley acted as a

00:07:38.940 --> 00:07:40.660
kind of mentor to Ambrose.

00:07:40.660 --> 00:07:43.610
"My boy, how did you ever end up as part of
a plot to blow up the Vatican?"

00:07:43.610 --> 00:07:45.090
"A young Crowley.

00:07:45.090 --> 00:07:48.910
He was brilliant, charismatic, and devoted
to the Dark Lord."

00:07:48.910 --> 00:07:54.250
In real life, Aleister Crowley was an English
occultist who gained notoriety for many things,

00:07:54.250 --> 00:07:59.670
including establishing the religion of Thelema,
aspects of which have inspired Wicca and Satanism.

00:07:59.670 --> 00:08:04.350
And like in the show, Crowley did actually
live in Loch Ness for a period of his life.

00:08:04.350 --> 00:08:09.300
The show's nine circles of hell are inspired
by Dante's Inferno, a drawing of which appears

00:08:09.300 --> 00:08:13.440
in the background on a school blackboard in
the first episode, another clue that by the

00:08:13.440 --> 00:08:17.990
end of Part 3, Sabrina will travel all the
way to the Ninth Circle of Hell.

00:08:17.990 --> 00:08:23.260
In Dante's epic poem, the Ninth Circle is
reserved for people who've committed treachery,

00:08:23.260 --> 00:08:24.470
including Judas Iscariot.

00:08:24.470 --> 00:08:29.310
So, it's fitting that that's where Caliban
tricks Sabrina and betrays her trust.

00:08:29.310 --> 00:08:33.849
On top of that, the Ninth Circle is also where
Sabrina breaks the promise she made to future

00:08:33.849 --> 00:08:38.379
Sabrina to complete the time loop by taking
her place in the stone prison.

00:08:38.379 --> 00:08:42.699
By the way, the fact that Chilling Adventures
encases its traitors in stone is another hat

00:08:42.699 --> 00:08:47.060
tip to Dante's Inferno where most of those
condemned to Hell's Ninth Circle are trapped

00:08:47.060 --> 00:08:48.610
in ice.

00:08:48.610 --> 00:08:52.939
Also in Ms Wardwell's classroom is another
blackboard where you can spot a mention of

00:08:52.939 --> 00:08:55.519
"Paradise Lost", an epic poem by John Milton.

00:08:55.519 --> 00:08:59.910
It was in "Paradise Lost" that Milton coined
the term "Pandemonium" for the capital of

00:08:59.910 --> 00:09:00.910
Hell.

00:09:00.910 --> 00:09:05.959
Not only is Pandemonium a crucial location
in Part 3, but Caliban himself is also sculpted

00:09:05.959 --> 00:09:07.769
from the city's clay.

00:09:07.769 --> 00:09:12.110
The backstory for Herod's Crown also notably
connects to the history of one of Riverdale's

00:09:12.110 --> 00:09:14.569
most significant families, the Blossoms.

00:09:14.569 --> 00:09:20.199
In Part 3, Ambrose discovers this first item
of the Unholy Regalia was passed between numerous

00:09:20.199 --> 00:09:24.639
people, the last known one being:
"Private Benjamin Blossom who recovered the

00:09:24.639 --> 00:09:27.720
crown from Hitler's bunker in 1945."

00:09:27.720 --> 00:09:31.259
Interestingly, Ambrose goes on to explain
that when Benjamin Blossom brought Herod's

00:09:31.259 --> 00:09:35.910
Crown back to Riverdale, he was murdered by
a group of occultists who wanted possession

00:09:35.910 --> 00:09:38.069
of the magical unholy relic.

00:09:38.069 --> 00:09:41.959
When Sabrina and Ambrose visit Riverdale to
locate the crown, they discover it's hidden

00:09:41.959 --> 00:09:46.079
in a maple syrup tree, which is especially
fitting because maple syrup has been part

00:09:46.079 --> 00:09:48.269
of the Blossom family business.

00:09:48.269 --> 00:09:52.980
In fact, the connection between the Blossoms
and King Herod seems particularly appropriate

00:09:52.980 --> 00:09:57.660
as history and myth remembers Herod for having
executed numerous male children including

00:09:57.660 --> 00:09:59.310
several of his own sons.

00:09:59.310 --> 00:10:05.100
And, of course, season 1 spoilers for Riverdale,
that show kicks off with the murder of Jason

00:10:05.100 --> 00:10:08.879
Blossom, who it's later revealed was killed
by his own father who was using the family

00:10:08.879 --> 00:10:12.230
syrup business as a front for selling drugs.

00:10:12.230 --> 00:10:16.670
It's interesting that actor Jonathan Whitesell
who plays Robin the Hobgoblin in Sabrina also

00:10:16.670 --> 00:10:19.009
played the part of Kurtz on Riverdale.

00:10:19.009 --> 00:10:21.390
Kurtz was a member of the Gargoyle Gang.

00:10:21.390 --> 00:10:26.480
But how can the same actor play two different
characters in two shows that are supposedly

00:10:26.480 --> 00:10:27.480
connected?

00:10:27.480 --> 00:10:31.730
Well, perhaps it could be another example
of the recurring theme of twins in both shows?

00:10:31.730 --> 00:10:35.529
In Chilling Adventures, there's the Blackwood
twins, Principal Hawthorne's twin who was

00:10:35.529 --> 00:10:40.510
absorbed in the womb, the image of Hilda and
Zelda as conjoined twins, and now, after much

00:10:40.510 --> 00:10:43.810
hinting in previous seasons, Sabrina has a
double too!

00:10:43.810 --> 00:10:48.850
Or perhaps it's all part of the shape-shifting
ability of Puck or Robin Goodfellow characters

00:10:48.850 --> 00:10:50.769
in English folklore?

00:10:50.769 --> 00:10:54.990
When Sabrina approaches Jimmy Platt's ice
cream truck, you can see it reads "A Chilling

00:10:54.990 --> 00:10:55.990
Adventure".

00:10:55.990 --> 00:10:59.800
That isn't just a play on the title of the
show though; it's also a hint at the chilly

00:10:59.800 --> 00:11:04.509
fate that awaits Sabrina later in the episode
when she ends up trapped in the evil ice cream

00:11:04.509 --> 00:11:05.740
seller's freezer.

00:11:05.740 --> 00:11:11.329
Curiously the same actor who plays Jimmy Platt,
is also going to appear on an episode of Riverdale

00:11:11.329 --> 00:11:12.759
as a quiz show host.

00:11:12.759 --> 00:11:16.450
This again raises the question of how the
same actor can play different characters in

00:11:16.450 --> 00:11:17.740
a shared universe.

00:11:17.740 --> 00:11:21.759
Previously, in an interview with Entertainment
Tonight, Chilling Adventures and Riverdale

00:11:21.759 --> 00:11:26.860
showrunner Roberto Aguirre-Sacasa explained
how Ben, a character who's already dead in

00:11:26.860 --> 00:11:30.519
Riverdale, later showed up as a pizza delivery
guy in Greendale.

00:11:30.519 --> 00:11:35.970
According to Aguirre-Sacasa, Ben's cameo "suggests
a very deep mythology where time and space

00:11:35.970 --> 00:11:36.970
bend."

00:11:36.970 --> 00:11:41.639
And even though Ben was dead in Riverdale,
"in Greendale, everyone pops up - the dead

00:11:41.639 --> 00:11:43.690
don't stay dead long [there]".

00:11:43.690 --> 00:11:47.459
There's an amusing reference to the crazy
events that go on in Greendale's neighbouring

00:11:47.459 --> 00:11:50.320
town when we see the "Welcome to Riverdale"
sign.

00:11:50.320 --> 00:11:55.069
On the back you can spot some Jughead graffiti
which dubs the town "Murder capital of the

00:11:55.069 --> 00:11:56.069
world".

00:11:56.069 --> 00:12:00.949
And in the Riverdale spin-off show Katy Keene,
Josie also refers to her hometown in the same

00:12:00.949 --> 00:12:01.949
way.

00:12:01.949 --> 00:12:02.949
"I am from Riverdale.

00:12:02.949 --> 00:12:04.329
It is the murder capital of the world."

00:12:04.329 --> 00:12:09.449
After Hilda turns into Spider-Hilda, she asks
Dr Cee to get her a hamburger and a milkshake

00:12:09.449 --> 00:12:14.809
from a diner in Riverdale, undoubtedly referencing
everyone's favourite meeting place in Riverdale,

00:12:14.809 --> 00:12:16.509
Pop's Chock'Lit Shoppe.

00:12:16.509 --> 00:12:21.140
Spider-Hilda also ends up eating a Riverdale
Southside Serpent gang member who wanders

00:12:21.140 --> 00:12:24.999
into Dr Cee's bookstore looking for something
to eat.

00:12:24.999 --> 00:12:29.110
Another Riverdale actor who makes an appearance
on Chilling Adventures is Nathalie Boltt,

00:12:29.110 --> 00:12:34.279
aka Penelope Blossom, spoilers for Riverdale,
the nefarious mastermind behind the Black

00:12:34.279 --> 00:12:36.279
Hood and the Gargoyle King.

00:12:36.279 --> 00:12:38.600
In Chilling Adventures, she pops up in New
Orleans.

00:12:38.600 --> 00:12:44.199
However, it turns out it's not the real Penelope
Blossom, but rather Prudence who's using Penelope's

00:12:44.199 --> 00:12:48.329
form for a glamour trick while she and Ambrose
are on the hunt for Blackwood.

00:12:48.329 --> 00:12:52.670
The title of the final episode, "Sabrina Is
Legend", is an intriguing reference to the

00:12:52.670 --> 00:12:57.220
2007 movie "I Am Legend", based on the book
of the same name.

00:12:57.220 --> 00:13:01.429
The movie is known for its alternate ending
in which, spoilers for the film, Will Smith

00:13:01.429 --> 00:13:05.199
gets a happier ending than the original one
shown in cinemas.

00:13:05.199 --> 00:13:10.110
Likewise in Chilling Adventures, Sabrina creates
an alternate and happier timeline for herself

00:13:10.110 --> 00:13:14.860
when she decides not to complete the time
loop as future Sabrina advised.

00:13:14.860 --> 00:13:18.990
And if you want to know much more about the
consequences Sabrina will face in Part 4 as

00:13:18.990 --> 00:13:22.829
a result of altering the timeline, watch my
Ending Explained video.

00:13:22.829 --> 00:13:26.230
You can tap the link here or click the link
in the video description.

00:13:26.230 --> 00:13:30.060
So, did you spot any other cool details or
references in Part 3?

00:13:30.060 --> 00:13:32.759
And what were your favourite moments this
season?

00:13:32.759 --> 00:13:34.759
Leave your thoughts in the comments below.

00:13:34.759 --> 00:13:38.309
If you enjoyed this, then a like and a share
are hugely appreciated.

00:13:38.309 --> 00:13:42.699
Tap left for my next Sabrina video or tap
right for another video you're sure to like.

00:13:42.699 --> 00:13:44.910
Thanks for watching and see ya next time.

00:13:44.910 --> 00:13:45.899
Yippee-ki-yay, movie lovers!

